<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46615" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭpĕr-ăbundo</span></b> ,
			āvi, 1, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to be very
			abundant</i>, <i>to superabound</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ubi delictum abundaverit, illic gratiam
					superabundasse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Res. Carn. 34</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">47</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn. Scip. 1,
				14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lact. Ep. 6, 13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Dig. 27, 1,
				6</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sŭpĕrăbundanter</span></b> ,
				adv., <i>very abundantly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facere omnia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Eph. 3, 20</span></i>
			.</div>
